5.2 Case study number 2 – quality of optimization convergence
It is inevitable that the final solutions from different runs using different initial GA populations are not identical, due to the large number of design variables and the stochastic nature of GA. The optimization problem in case study number 1 is repeated ten times and the variations in the optimal results from the multiple runs reveal that the difference between the worst and best results is only 11 per cent, acceptable for engineering practicality (Table 10).
